## Manual Replay Walkthrough

Step-by-step commands to apply the manifest manually, without the Runner.

### Step 1 — Start the stack

```bash
docker-compose up -d
```

### Step 2 — Wait for services to be ready

```bash
echo "Waiting for auth-service..."
until curl -sf http://localhost:8080/health >/dev/null; do sleep 1; done
echo "auth-service ready"

echo "Waiting for inventory-service..."
until curl -sf http://localhost:9090/health >/dev/null; do sleep 1; done
echo "inventory-service ready"

echo "Waiting for gateway-api..."
until curl -sf http://localhost:9000/health >/dev/null; do sleep 1; done
echo "gateway-api ready"
```

### Step 3 — Source credentials

```bash
set -a
. ./.data-seed-credentials.env
set +a
```

### Step 4 — Apply auth-service steps in order

```bash
# Create test org
psql "${AUTH_SERVICE_DB_URL}" -f data-seed/auth-service/001-orgs.sql

# Create test user (-v passes the plaintext password so it never lives in a checked-in file)
psql "${AUTH_SERVICE_DB_URL}" -v test_pass="${TEST_PASS}" -f data-seed/auth-service/002-users.sql

# Link user to org
psql "${AUTH_SERVICE_DB_URL}" -f data-seed/auth-service/003-memberships.sql
```

### Step 5 — Apply inventory-service steps

```bash
psql "${INVENTORY_SERVICE_DB_URL}" -f data-seed/inventory-service/001-apps.sql
```

### Step 6 — Apply gateway-api steps (manual curl translation of the .http file)

```bash
# Login — extract session cookie from response headers
SESSION=$(curl -s -D - -X POST "${GATEWAY_URL}/login" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d "{\"email\":\"${TEST_USER}\",\"password\":\"${TEST_PASS}\"}" \
  | grep -i "set-cookie: session=" \
  | sed 's/.*session=\([^;]*\).*/\1/' \
  | tr -d '[:space:]')

echo "Session cookie: ${SESSION}"

# Create Development env for target-app-1 (idempotent via PUT)
curl -s -X PUT "${GATEWAY_URL}/v1/apps/target-app-1/envs/Development" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Cookie: session=${SESSION}" \
  -d "{
    \"host\": \"http://localhost:9000\",
    \"applicationId\": \"${TEST_APP_ID}\"
  }"
```

