## Validation — What Success Looks Like

Run these after applying the seed. Each must return the expected result.

### auth-service — org exists

```bash
psql "${AUTH_SERVICE_DB_URL}" -c \
  "SELECT 1 FROM organizations WHERE id='00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001';"
# Expected: 1 row
```

### auth-service — user exists

```bash
psql "${AUTH_SERVICE_DB_URL}" -c \
  "SELECT 1 FROM users WHERE email='test-owner@example.com';"
# Expected: 1 row
```

### auth-service — membership exists

```bash
psql "${AUTH_SERVICE_DB_URL}" -c \
  "SELECT 1 FROM user_org_memberships
   WHERE user_id='00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002'
     AND org_id='00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001';"
# Expected: 1 row
```

### inventory-service — app exists

```bash
psql "${INVENTORY_SERVICE_DB_URL}" -c \
  "SELECT 1 FROM applications WHERE name='target-app-1';"
# Expected: 1 row
```

### gateway-api — env link exists

> Requires the `SESSION` cookie obtained in Manual Replay Step 6. Run that step first.

```bash
curl -s -H "Cookie: session=${SESSION}" \
  "${GATEWAY_URL}/v1/apps/target-app-1/envs" | jq '.envs | length'
# Expected: ≥ 1
```

### Idempotency check

Re-run all seed steps. Then re-run the validation commands. Row counts must not
change.

### HawkScan authentication check

After seeding, with `.data-seed-credentials.env` sourced, HawkScan configured
against the running gateway should authenticate successfully and find > 1 path:

```bash
set -a; . ./.data-seed-credentials.env; set +a
hawk scan   # or: hawkscan --config stackhawk.yml
```

A successful scan completes without a 401/403 and reports at least the `/login`
route plus one or more `/v1/*` routes.
